sec.p:
As an example, let Gravity-IndexSRlow(respectively Gravity-IndexSRmedium and Gravity-IndexSRhigh) be the averaged index for success rates for low-gravity-dependent games (respectively medium-gravity-dependent games, high-dependent-gravity games) for a participant.


 Gravity-Index SRlow=(averageSRGVSlow−averageSRSham low)(averageSRGVSlow+averageSRSham low)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \text { Gravity-Index }_{S R_{\text {low }}}=\frac{\left(\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{G V S_{\text {low }}}-\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{\text {Sham }}{ }_{\text {low }}\right)}{\left(\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{G V S_{\text {low }}}+\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{\text {Sham }_{\text {low }}}\right)}$$\end{document}





 Gravity-Index SRmedium=(averageSRGVSmedium−averageSRSham medium)(averageSRGVSmedium+averageSRSham medium)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \text { Gravity-Index }_{S R_{\text {medium }}}=\frac{\left(\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{G V S_{\text {medium }}}-\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{\text {Sham }}{ }_{\text {medium }}\right)}{\left(\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{G V S_{\text {medium }}}+\text { average } \mathrm{SR}_{\text {Sham }}{ }_{\text {medium }}\right)}$$\end{document}





 Gravity-Index SRhigh=(averageSRGVShigh−averageSRSham high)(averageSRGVShigh+averageSRSham high)
\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \text { Gravity-Index }_{S R_{\text {high }}}=\frac{\left(\text { average }_{S R_{G V S_{\text {high }}}-\text { average }_{\text {SR }} \text { Sham }_{\text {high }}}\right)}{\left(\mathrm{SR}_{G V S_{\text {high }}}+\mathrm{SR}_{S h a m_{\text {high }}}\right)}$$\end{document}



For success GI, a value close to -1 indicates a large negative difference between GVS and Sham gravity results, a value close to 0 similar results and a value close to 1 indicates a large positive difference between GVS and Sham gravity results.
